# HarnessFlow on Cursor

This workspace ships HarnessFlow: a constraint-based workflow for building software products. It does not script your steps — it defines seven invariants, three user checkpoints, and a product truth layout, then leaves the method to you.

## On every task that changes the product

1. Load `skills/harness/SKILL.md` first. It is the only binding document: invariants, checkpoints, the `product/` + `work/` truth layout, and the evidence protocol `skills/harness/scripts/harness.py`.
2. Cold-start from disk: read `product/` (intent, state, decisions, backlog), then unfinished lines under `work/`. Chat history is scratch paper, not memory. If `product/` does not exist yet, run `harness.py init` and start from the intent checkpoint.
3. Playbooks under `skills/harness/references/` (shaping, building, reviewing, releasing) are advice — deviating from them needs no approval; violating an invariant is never allowed.

## The invariants, in one breath

Truth lives on disk; claims need machine evidence (`harness.py run` into `work/<slug>/evidence/`, hand-editing logs is fabrication); a falsifiable success signal exists in `work/<slug>/signal.md` before the product changes; the verification entry in `product/state.md` always actually runs; the user owns what/whether (intent, tradeoffs, irreversible actions — the three checkpoints), you own how; nothing is declared done without an independent perspective (`work/<slug>/review.md`); prefer reversible moves.

Pure Q&A or code-reading requests that change nothing do not need HarnessFlow.
